      "statement": "H5771G/H/I are one Hebrew lexeme (avon) split into three catalogue entries purely by which of its meaning block's own three listed sub-senses ('iniquity'/'guilt of iniquity'/'consequence or punishment for iniquity') a given occurrence was assigned to -- the split is a cataloguing convenience, not three different words. Reading all three together (106 occurrences) shows the SAME three-part structure -- state, guilt-consequence, punishment-consequence -- that recurs identically in H6588 (pesha, family G) and the chattah root (family B), now confirmed a third time as the organizing structure the underlying reference lexicon applies uniformly to this whole semantic domain, not something specific to any one root's actual usage.",
